!Sample_organism_ch1 = Mus musculus
!Sample_taxid_ch1 = 10090
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = disease state: normal
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = cell line: normal bone marrow GMP
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = strain: C57BL/6
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = cell type: hematopoietic cells
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = time: 0hr (before)
!Sample_treatment_protocol_ch1 = RNA samples were prepared 0h, 6h and 10h after RG3039 treatment of cells
!Sample_molecule_ch1 = total RNA
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = RNA was extracted using an RNeasy Mini Kit (Qiagen).
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = Libraries were generated using the Ovation Mouse RNA-Seq System following the manufacturer’s specifications (NuGEN)
!Sample_description = Processed data in Series supplementary file Rna-seq DCPS.xlsx
!Sample_data_processing = Mouse reference mm10 using STAR aligner
!Sample_data_processing = We assessed individual junction counts for each cohort by summing these counts over all samples in that cohort. Estimation of intron retention counts were performed by defining a 6 nt window over each exon-exon junction (3 nt in exon and 3 nt in intron), and all reads which completely overlapped this window were considered intronic (Darman et al., 2015) Individual junction usage in each cohort was then converted to a percent spliced in (PSI) measurement by dividing the count of that junction by the total count of all junctions sharing a splice site with it in that cohort. We assessed differential junction PSI between cohorts using a binomial z-test, and p-values were corrected using FDR. A q-value < 0.05 was considered significant.
!Sample_data_processing = Genome_build: mm10
!Sample_platform_id = GPL19057
